# Component-Driven Architecture

## Pages are Server Components
- No `"use client"` in `page.tsx`
- Export `metadata` from the page
- Pages stay thin: read cookies or catalog data, then render one feature component
- Missing products use `notFound()`

## Feature components
- Interactive UI lives in `src/features/<domain>/components/*-content.tsx`
- Mark those files `"use client"`
- Domains: `auth`, `home`, `category`, `product`, `cart`, `checkout`, `order`, `account`, `addresses`

```
src/app/(shop)/cart/page.tsx
src/features/cart/components/cart-content.tsx

src/app/(shop)/products/[id]/page.tsx
src/features/product/components/product-detail-content.tsx
```

## Page template

```tsx
import type { Metadata } from 'next';
import { CartContent } from '@/features/cart/components/cart-content';

export const metadata: Metadata = { title: 'سبد خرید | پلنتی' };

export default function CartPage() {
  return <CartContent />;
}
```

## Rules
1. Never put `"use client"` on `page.tsx`
2. One `h1` per screen; use `button` for actions and `Link` for navigation
3. Shop pages render inside `(shop)/layout.tsx` (phone frame + bottom nav)
4. Auth screens (`welcome`, `login`, `register`, `otp`) stay outside that layout
